// A non-UDT type declaration is the deliberate UNIT exception. The reference
// permits it "directly inside an ordinary unit" and prohibits it "physically
// inside classes, structs, modules, functions, or executable blocks".
//
// This shape is the reason the container probe cannot reuse the executable-block
// one: `name KIND = value` reads as a variable declarator in a block, so folding
// the type-declaration kinds in with the built-in data types let a class accept
// this silently, as a field named Alias carrying a default.
_ co.lang.class = {

    Alias co.lang.type = co.lang.int;

    getIt()->(co.lang.int) = { }
}
